# Vite names every file under /assets after its contents, so one never changes: the browser keeps it for the day
# and doesn't ask again. The page itself is still checked on every visit, and names the files it needs.
#
# A day, not the customary year, as first set (2026-10-07), when an address under /assets that named no file was
# answered with the app's page and this header with it. Since 2026-10-14 the Worker answers such an address with a 404
# that nothing keeps (worker/assets.ts), so this header goes only on files the build has.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, immutable
